BILDSCHIRMTRIX
===========================================================================================================
                                                                                           Online anno 1983
==Abstract==
Bildschirmtrix is a combination of hard and software that allows you to set up you own 
Bildschirmtext network. Bildschirmtrix brings the good old days back to your BTX-Terminal.


==Access via HTTP==
With the mikroPAD hardware you are able to use your existing http-server as a btx datacenter. 
BTX-Pages will be encoded as a html like hypertext pages so you can use your favourite script 
lanuguage to do the hypertext preprocessing (php, perl, ruby or whatever). And the best of all: 
The mikroPAD board exactly fits into an DBT-03 case.

All about the mikroPAD device can be found in ./mikroPAD

Note: The mikroPAD is based on the Mikrowebserver by Dirk Broßwick.

Also see folder ./pcPAD for a PAD-Software that runs on PCs


==DBT-02 to RS232==
Besides the very complex mikroPAD hardware device the project also includes an adapter that 
is easy to build and suitable for embedded projects (mikroPAD uses exactly that adaptor): 
miniBTX. The package also contains an example C-Program that illustrates how to handle the 
adapter and the CEPT page encoding which makes it ideal for testing and experimenting 
(I had to do many experiments to find out how BTX really works.)



==Exemples==
Exemple pages can be found in ./srv Just upload ./srv to an http server and have a lot of
fun with your mikroPAD.


==Tools==
I wrote some tools that make it easyer to create own BTX sites. You will find them in 
./tools 


==Protocol==

BTX-Terminals are working with the the CEPT T/CD 6-1 specification. Getting information 
about that CEPT-Protocol is a bit problematic, but not impossible if you know the magic 
words. You will find lots of useful information at http://www.etsi.org

The document numbers are:

T/TE 06-01 / T/CD 06-01  =  ETS 300 072
T/TE 06-01               =  ETS 300 073
T/TE 06-03               =  ETS 300 074
T/TE 06-04 / T/CD 06-04  =  ETS 300 075
T/TE 06-05 / T/CD 06-05  =  ETS 300 076


